1. Clone the ontology and ensure that it is built.
   For UCO and CASE this required a clone, and a 'make all' to ensure all ttl files are present

2. Using ontospy, run the serializer over the directory of the ontology, and output the console to an RDF file.

ontospy ser ../CASE/ontology/ --verbose -f xml > case.rdf
ontospy ser ../UCO/ontology/ --verbose -f xml > uco.rdf